<.page_shell flash={@flash}>
  <.legal_page eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" updated="17 July 2026">
    <p class="text-ink-muted text-lead font-light">
      Nila is operated by Kaguya Media Private Limited ("Nila", "we", "us").
      This policy explains what we collect, why, who processes it on our behalf,
      and the rights you have over it. It covers
      <span class="text-ink font-medium">nila.tax</span>
      and the Nila application. If anything here is unclear, write to <a
        href="mailto:privacy@nila.tax"
        class="hover:text-ink text-primary font-medium transition"
      >
        privacy@nila.tax
      </a>.
    </p>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Who the data belongs to</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        Our customers are CA firms and accountants. The documents you upload —
        bills, bank statements, GST returns — describe your clients' businesses.
        You are the data fiduciary for that material; Nila is a data processor
        acting on your instructions. We use it only to produce the workings you
        asked for, and never to build a product for anyone else.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">What we collect</h2>
      <ul class="marker:text-ink-faint text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 font-light">
        <li>
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Account data</span> — name, email,
          firm details, and authentication records for the people who log in.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Uploaded documents</span> — invoices,
          bank statements, GSTR files, photos, and anything else you send Nila to
          process, together with the structured records extracted from them
          (vendors, GSTINs, amounts, tax lines).
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Client and contact details</span> — the
          businesses and people your work concerns, including GSTINs, and the
          phone numbers or emails Nila uses to chase missing documents in your
          firm's name.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">WhatsApp communications</span> —
          incoming and outgoing messages, sender and recipient phone numbers,
          images, PDFs and other attachments, delivery and read statuses, message
          identifiers, and timestamps. We use this data to receive documents,
          follow up on missing records, and show your firm what happened.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Operational logs</span> — audit trails
          of actions taken in the app, and standard technical logs (IP, browser,
          timestamps) needed to run and secure the service.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Why we process it</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        To extract, classify, and draft the GST artifacts you use; to flag the
        lines that need a human; to follow up on missing documents on your behalf;
        to secure the service and keep an audit trail; and to meet our legal and
        tax obligations. We do not sell your data, and we do not use your clients'
        documents for advertising.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Who processes it for us</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        We use a small set of sub-processors under contract, each limited to what
        its job needs:
      </p>
      <ul class="marker:text-ink-faint text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 font-light">
        <li>
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Hosting</span> — our servers and
          database run on dedicated infrastructure (Hetzner) that we administer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Document processing / AI</span> —
          uploaded documents may be sent to third-party model providers solely to
          extract and structure their contents for your workings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="text-ink font-medium">Email &amp; messaging</span> —
          transactional email (Resend) and Meta's WhatsApp Cloud API, used to
          receive documents, notify you, report delivery status, and chase missing
          records.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        We will name our current sub-processors on request. Some may process data
        outside India; where they do, we rely on contractual safeguards.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        We retain documents and the records derived from them for as long as your
        account is active and you need them for your filings, plus the period
        required to meet legal and tax record-keeping obligations. When you close
        your account, we delete or anonymise your data within a reasonable period,
        except where law requires us to keep it longer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">How we protect it</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        Access is scoped per firm — one firm's documents are never served to
        another. Data is encrypted in transit, access is restricted to personnel
        who need it, and sensitive fields such as bank account numbers are stored
        encrypted. No system is perfectly secure, but we treat financial documents
        as sensitive by default.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        You can ask us to access, correct, export, or delete the personal data we
        hold about you, and to address grievances about how we handle it. Where you
        are acting for your clients, we will support you in meeting the
        corresponding requests from them. Write to
        <a
          href="mailto:privacy@nila.tax"
          class="hover:text-ink text-primary font-medium transition"
        >
          privacy@nila.tax
        </a>
        and we will respond within a reasonable period. See our
        <.link
          navigate={~p"/data-deletion"}
          class="hover:text-ink text-primary font-medium transition"
        >
          data deletion instructions
        </.link>
        to make a deletion request.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Changes</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        We may update this policy as the service evolves. Material changes will be
        posted here with a new date; continued use after a change means you accept
        the updated policy.
      </p>
    </section>
  </.legal_page>
</.page_shell>
